            <ArticleTitle>Amiodarone-induced dysthyroidism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>610-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 54-year-old man, treated with amiodarone, developed thyrotoxicosis. When rechallenged with the same drug 6 months later, he developed hypothyroidism. The therapeutic implications of this clinical sequence are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
